An '''Imperial factory facility''' was run by the [[Galactic Empire]]<ref name="JKE" /> on [[Narkina 2]]<ref name="Insider223" /> in the [[Narkina system]] of the [[Outer Rim Territories]]' [[Abrion sector]].<ref name="Appendix">{{GalaxyMapAppendix}} &mdash; Based on corresponding data for the [[Narkina system]]</ref> After being found to have acquired confidential files relating to [[Project Stardust]] that she did not have clearance for<ref name="Who Else">{{Andor|Who Else Knows?}}</ref> in [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{AndorDate|212}}</ref> former [[Imperial Security Bureau]] [[ISB Supervisor|supervisor]]<ref name="Who Else" /> [[Dedra Meero]] was [[Prisoner|incarcerated]] in the [[Imperial factory facility]]. Following a shift at the prison during her incarceration, Meero sat in her cellblock and remained composed until the lights in her cellblock turned off&mdash;after which she broke down crying.<ref name="JKE" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|It's probably Narkina 7 or Narkina 2. It's the women's version.|Tony Gilroy, on Dedra Meero's prison|<ref name="EW">{{WebCite|url=https://ew.com/andor-creator-tony-gilroy-explains-surprise-ending-final-shot-11731474|text=''Andor'' creator Tony Gilroy explains that surprise ending and final shot|author=Dalton Ross|date=2025-05-14|archivedate=20250516141415}}</ref>}}
The Imperial factory facility first appeared in "[[Jedha, Kyber, Erso]],"<ref name="JKE" /> the series finale of the [[Disney+]] live-action television series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'', which was released on [[May 13]], [[2025]].<ref name="Insider223">{{InsiderCite|233|Andor Season 2 Companion|''Andor'' Season 2 Companion}}</ref>

When discussing the prison in an [[Wikipedia:Entertainment Weekly|''Entertainment Weekly'']] interview published on [[May 14]], 2025, Andor's creator [[Tony Gilroy]] described Meero's prison as hypothetically being [[Narkina 2]] or Narkina 7 as an [[Gender|all-female]] prison<ref name="EW" /> as opposed to [[Narkina 5]], the location of an [[Unidentified Imperial factory facility|Imperial factory facility]] seen in [[Andor Season 1|''Andor'' Season 1]].<ref name="Narkina 5">{{Andor|Narkina 5 (episode)}}</ref><ref name="EW" /> In a [[StarWars.com]] written by [[Kristin Baver]] published the same day as the interview, the prison was stated to be "reminiscent of Narkina 2,"<ref name="Explained">{{SW|url=news/andor-season-2-finale-episodes-10-11-12|text=''Andor'' Explained: Episodes 10-12 - "Make It Stop", "Who Else Knows?", and "Jedha, Kyber, Erso"}}</ref> a typo of Narkina 5.<ref name="Narkina 5" /> The location of the Imperial factory facility being Narkina 2 was eventually confirmed in the ''[[Star Wars Insider]]'' magazine article [[Andor Season 2 Companion|''Andor'' Season 2 Companion]] by [[Lucas O. Seastrom]] and [[Jay Stobie (real person)|Jay Stobie]] published in [[Star Wars Insider 233|''Star Wars Insider'' 233]]<ref name="Insider223">{{InsiderCite|233|Andor Season 2 Companion|''Andor'' Season 2 Companion}}</ref> on [[August 19]], 2025.<ref name="Titan">{{TitanComics|url=m/183-star-wars-insider-233|text=Star Wars Insider #233}}</ref>

